---
import "../styles/global.css";

const install = "curl -fsSL https://fidelius.ashray.xyz/install.sh | bash";
const ask = `fidelius \\
  -s restaurant-scraping-demo \\
  -m "I need the Google Maps API key to finish scraping restaurant menus." \\
  GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`;
const retrieve = `security find-generic-password \\
  -s restaurant-scraping-demo \\
  -a GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY \\
  -w`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Fidelius lets agents ask humans for secrets and saves them to macOS Keychain." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Fidelius — secrets from humans to agents</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav shell">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Fidelius home">
        <img src="/app-icon.svg" alt="" />
        <span>Fidelius</span>
      </a>
      <a class="github" href="https://github.com/amxv/fidelius">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero shell">
        <p class="kicker">A tiny macOS utility for agents</p>
        <h1>Agents ask.<br /><span>You paste.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">
          Fidelius gives agents a native way to ask you for secrets. Paste once, save to macOS Keychain,
          and let the agent keep working without putting credentials in chat or sending you to the terminal.
        </p>
        <div class="install" aria-label="Install Fidelius">
          <code>{install}</code>
          <button data-copy={install}>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p class="meta">macOS 13+ · Apple Silicon + Intel · open source</p>

        <div class="product-shot">
          <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <img src="/fidelius-window.png" alt="The real Fidelius macOS window requesting a Google Maps API key" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story shell">
        <div class="story-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">A realistic handoff</p>
          <h2>The moment an agent gets blocked, it asks you.</h2>
          <p>
            No provider integration. No new secret store. Just one Unix command that waits for the human part.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example Fidelius command">
          <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <pre><code>{ask}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="keychain-band">
        <div class="shell keychain-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Keychain stays the source of truth</p>
            <h2>Fidelius does one thing, then gets out of the way.</h2>
            <p>
              Once you save, the secret is an ordinary generic password in macOS Keychain. Agents keep using Apple's
              familiar <code>security</code> CLI and normal Unix composition.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="code-card">
            <span>Read it later</span>
            <pre><code>{retrieve}</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="features shell">
        <article>
          <div class="feature-icon">⌘</div>
          <h3>Wait as long as you need.</h3>
          <p>The prompt is a normal Mac app window. Cmd-Tab away, provision the secret, and come back when you're ready.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="feature-icon">•••</div>
          <h3>Ask for several at once.</h3>
          <p>One invocation can request multiple named secrets without exposing any of their values to the agent.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="feature-icon">Ⅱ</div>
          <h3>Parallel agents are fine.</h3>
          <p>Each invocation owns its own window, so several agents can wait on independent Fidelius prompts at the same time.</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="closing shell">
        <img src="/app-icon.svg" alt="" />
        <h2>A tiny human interface for agent credentials.</h2>
        <div class="install install-bottom">
          <code>{install}</code>
          <button data-copy={install}>Copy</button>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="shell">
      <span>Fidelius</span>
      <div>
        <a href="https://github.com/amxv/fidelius">GitHub</a>
        <span>Apache-2.0</span>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
          const value = button.getAttribute("data-copy");
          if (!value) return;
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value);
          const original = button.textContent;
          button.textContent = "Copied";
          setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = original; }, 1200);
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
